  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 332 AM MDT SAT AUG 1 2026\nThe Desert Southwest upper-level ridge will be, yet again,\ndriving the synoptic pattern. Clusters have the extent of the\nhighest 500 mb heights associated with the ridge reaching to\nthe California coast, thereby limiting any monsoonal moisture \nfrom getting north to our region. Thus, hot and dry conditions \nare expected to return and stick around. By Wednesday, highs \nare back into the mid-upper 90s/near 100 degrees across lower \nelevations (smoke coverage/density dependent). There is no \nchance for precipitation through the period as monsoonal \nmoisture remains bottled up over the Four Corners region.",
